ing a National Geographic investigation into the destruction of Pompeii in AD79 (Disney+, from Thursday), there was no way I wasnâ€™t watching.</p><p>The actor has famously sauntered through lifeâ€™s most vaunted way stations: Eton, Cambridge, Rada, <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/film/2017/mar/12/kong-skull-island-review-tom-hiddlestone-unsubtle-adventure">Kong: Skull Island</a>. Privilege and perceived smugness have long been sticks to beat him with. Itâ€™s harder to argue heâ€™s not qualified for this job, having earned a double first in classics. Here, he slips into the role of undergraduate detective. A&nbsp;real-life scholar is forced to cosplay as his don during their interview, addressing Hiddleston by surname, issuing prim little reprimands. Hiddleston even translates Latin headstones in the first episode. I&nbsp;donâ€™t know what the ancient Roman for â€œscrew it, Iâ€™m leaning inâ€ is, but I think thatâ€™s what it means.</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2026/jul/18/pompeii-out-of-time-with-tom-hiddleston-tearjerking-television-disney">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;WH8teqDl1kXFNhjH83P-GYLNJIOKHtZDEb9F9O341uIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxvPompeii: Out of Time With Tom Hiddleston â€“ the tale of ordinary Romansâ€™ hopeless heroism is tearjerking televisionƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;eIobn5wUcEvyr0HEjw1ktpwwdC9MoFHrKmODw-im9OQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkoSyndicationItemƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;sG3BXtbgkvTEdIE741hdDY3nalDAV26nwq5cGuzDuAkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxzhttps://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2026/jul/18/pompeii-out-of-time-with-tom-hiddleston-tearjerking-television-disneyƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha